 GATE 3b ITEM 7: DEPENDENCY GRAPH ADD/REMOVE SENSITIVITY & ABLATION
================================================================================
 Mathematical Sensitivity Derivation Analysis:
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1. Under ADD/REMOVE adjacency, dataset sizes differ: |D| = N, |D'| = N +/- 1.
 2. The dependency matrix R uses composite statistics (Pearson + Spearman rank
    correlation, mutual information, ANOVA F-ratios, and random downsampling).
 3. For Spearman rank correlation, inserting 1 record shifts the ranks of up to
    N existing records by +/- 1, making worst-case sensitivity data-dependent.
 4. Mutual information and ANOVA F-ratios have unbounded sensitivity without
    data-dependent smooth sensitivity or heuristic clipping.
 5. Per Gate 3b Item 7: As exact add/remove sensitivity cannot be derived formally
    for this composite estimator, we replace the noised graph with the public-only
    ontology graph and move the freed 0.08 epsilon entirely to DP-SGD training.
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

